# 4. P0 — Permission / Sandbox / Process

## 4.1 Capability-Based Permissions

* [x] Enable Capability Model as the primary permission system — agent-dispatch makes PermissionRuntime::decide the single decision point for every tool call; a call outside the grant's scope does not run
* [x] Tool Capability — ToolMetadata::capabilities is what capability_for reads; a tool declaring nothing falls back by risk level rather than being waved through
* [x] File Capability — consulted on every file call, with relative paths resolved against the workspace first so a scope check decides the file that would actually be opened
* [~] Command Capability — same, and run_command is the call that most needs it
* [x] MCP Capability — mcp.call goes through PermissionRuntime::decide against Resource::Name(server). Enforced only once the host declares a policy, so an older host is not broken; see §0.2 F7
* [x] Sub-agent Capability — subagent.spawn derives its grant through issue_child from the session ceiling rather than hardcoding Grant::empty(); elevated kinds are stripped and depth starves out
* [x] Capability Scope — kind + scope, matched component-wise so /home/u/proj does not cover /home/u/project-secrets
* [x] Permission Denied Result — in the crate
* [x] Permission Audit — PermissionRuntime audits every decision it makes, and sandbox decisions are published as events

Example:

```text
write_file
    ↓
Scope:
/project/**
```

Instead of:

```text
write_file
    ↓
Full filesystem access
```

## 4.2 Sandbox

* [x] Linux Landlock integration — agent-sandbox, applied in the child between fork and exec; differential escape proof
* [x] Filesystem Scope enforcement
* [x] Symlink protection
* [x] Path Traversal protection
* [x] Sandbox Escape Tests — 11 tests that attempt real escapes against a confined child
* [x] Grandchild Process Escape Tests
* [x] Sandbox Failure Handling — reports Enforcement::None with the reason rather than pretending

## 4.3 Process Manager

* [x] Process Spawn
* [x] Process Group
* [x] Child Process Tracking
* [x] Grandchild Process Tracking
* [x] SIGTERM handling
* [x] Grace Period — 2s
* [x] SIGKILL fallback
* [x] Zombie Process Reaping — every child is awaited by construction; asserted across 40 sequential runs
* [~] CPU Limits — cgroups v2 first, setrlimit fallback; Windows Job Objects not implemented
* [~] Memory Limits — same
* [~] Process Limits — same
* [x] Resource Cleanup

### Final Execution Chain

```text
Agent
 ↓
Permission
 ↓
Capability Scope
 ↓
Sandbox
 ↓
Process Manager
 ↓
Tool
 ↓
OS
```

