# 6. P1 — Sub-agent Runtime

## 6.1 Actor Model

* [x] Sub-agent Actor
* [x] Independent lifecycle
* [x] Independent state
* [x] Independent cancellation
* [x] Independent timeout
* [x] Independent error handling
* [x] Error isolation — a panicking delegation becomes that job's Failed outcome; siblings finish normally
* [~] Capability isolation — derive_child exists in agent-permission and the supervisor does not use it
* [x] Concurrency limits — 4, process-wide
* [x] Quota control

## 6.2 Sub-agent Scheduling

```text
Main Agent
     │
     ▼
Scheduler
 ┌───┼────┐
 ↓   ↓    ↓
Explore Plan Coder
 │    │    │
Actor Actor Actor
```

Sub-agents must not automatically inherit elevated capabilities from the Main Agent.

## 6.3 Sub-agent Results

* [x] Standardized Result
* [x] Error Result
* [x] Partial Result — 2s grace on cancel, so a stopped delegation can still report a partial conclusion
* [x] Cancellation Result
* [x] Runtime Events — delivered as `runtime.event` notifications; onRuntimeEvent() in the host bridge
* [~] UI State Synchronization — the events reach the host and can be subscribed to; no UI consumes them yet

