# 7. P1 — MCP Runtime

## 7.1 MCP Supervisor

* [x] MCP Server Registry
* [x] MCP Connection Management
* [x] MCP Discovery
* [x] MCP Tool Discovery
* [x] Heartbeat — detects a silently-dead server before a tool call does
* [x] Automatic Reconnect — runs in the supervisor's own loop, not lazily on the next call
* [x] Exponential Backoff
* [x] Timeout — a per-call timeout does not tear the connection down
* [x] Concurrent Calls
* [x] Backpressure — per-connection in-flight limit plus a response size cap
* [x] MCP Process Management

## 7.2 MCP Permissions

All MCP Tools must use the same Capability system:

```text
Agent
 ↓
MCP Supervisor
 ↓
Capability Check
 ↓
MCP Tool
 ↓
External Application
```

Example:

```text
Zeraix
 ↓
MCP
 ↓
Blender
```

MCP must not bypass Runtime Permission, Sandbox, or Audit mechanisms.

