# 15. Final 2.0 Architecture Acceptance

The final architecture should be:

```text
                  User
                   │
                   ▼
             Electron UI
                   │
                  IPC
                   │
                   ▼
          Rust Agent Runtime
                   │
        ┌──────────┼──────────┐
        ▼          ▼          ▼
     Agent      Scheduler   Context
      Core
        │
        ▼
       Tool
        │
   ┌────┼─────┐
   ▼    ▼     ▼
Permission Sandbox Process
   │    │     │
   └────┼─────┘
        ▼
   Tool / MCP
        │
        ▼
        OS
```

The following must be true:

* [~] Agent execution is controlled by Rust Runtime — TOOL execution is, with no fallback. The agent LOOP still runs in TypeScript; agent.run exists and nothing calls it yet
* [~] Tool execution is controlled by Rust Runtime — tools, commands, MCP and sub-agents only
* [x] Permission is enforced by Runtime — every tool call through agent-dispatch, every MCP call unconditionally (§0.2 F7 resolved 2026-09-01)
* [x] Sandbox is enforced by Runtime — on Linux, where Landlock provides it; still nothing on Windows or macOS (see §0.2 F4)
* [x] Processes are managed by Runtime
* [x] Scheduler manages Tasks
* [x] Scheduler manages Sub-agents
* [x] MCP is managed by Runtime
* [~] Context State can be persisted — TaskMemory is a serialisable record and task lifecycle is durable (agent-journal); nothing writes the conversation to disk yet
* [x] Compaction preserves critical task state — structurally: task memory lives outside the conversation compaction operates on
* [~] Electron does not directly control core Agent execution — it no longer EXECUTES tools or commands, having no implementation left to do it with; it still drives the loop
* [x] Runtime can recover from crashes — the process restarts and reports the previous run's unfinished work, distinguishing what is safe to resume from what may already have had side effects
* [~] Core execution behavior is auditable — on the TypeScript side
* [~] Security Tests pass — the sandbox and permission suites pass; several rows in §12 have no suite
* [x] Long-running Agent Tests pass — agent-loop/tests/stress.rs: 200 rounds, 120 fanned-out tool calls, and 60 rounds of sustained compaction, each asserting consistency at the end rather than a timing

